# Input graph for fair-workflows__fairworkflows__fairworkflows_rdf_wrapper.py__RdfWrapper__uri_is_subject_in_rdf — written during translation.
# It must cover: several solutions of the pattern the region reads (a
# subject with more than one triple), the zero-solution case (a URI queried
# by driver.py that never appears as a subject here), and neighbouring
# triples that must NOT match (a URI that only appears as an OBJECT, never
# as a subject), and a URI used only as a PREDICATE (ex:p, queried by
# driver.py: must not count as a subject either).
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

ex:present ex:p "v1" ;
           ex:q "v2" .

ex:other ex:p ex:onlyAnObject .

# a subject whose only triple uses another predicate and an IRI object:
# with ex:present and ex:other, kills a predicate or object narrowed from
# the wildcard
ex:onlyQ ex:q ex:somewhere .
